{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789237488,"nonce":"2pW1qfOMV7HLJyIUusBHpCSzSZ4=","title":"An unannotated let whose type the typed AST does not know is recorded as the dynamic box type","message":"The SSA pre-scan (`scan_cfg_for_variable_types`) converts each let's\ndeclared type into var_types before translation. A let with `Type::Any`\nor `Type::Unknown` (a frontend that leaves inference to the value, or a\nZynML `let` the resolver could not type) converts to the DynamicBox\npointer type, so every phi joining that variable across blocks is typed\nas a box pointer while the value flowing in is an i64, an f64 or a list\nheader.\n\nReproducer: a Python loop accumulating into a variable first assigned\nfrom a list index (`s = xs[0]; for ...: s = s + xs[i]`) with the element\ntype known only to the value.\n\nFix: the pre-scan skips such lets, and the Let translation records the\ntype of the value actually held (falling back to convert_type when the\nvalue has no type).","files":null}]}